From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 17:39:58 +0200
Subject: media: cedrus: Implement AFBC YUV420 output for VP9

The H616 video engine can emit its primary reconstruction output as an
ARM Frame Buffer Compression (AFBC) surface instead of plain NV12/P010,
which is more memory-bandwidth efficient. Wire this up for VP9:

- Add the VE mode-register compression bits (COMPRESS_EN, MIN_VAL_WRAP_EN,
  RGB_DEF_COLOR_EN, BODYBUF_1K_ALIGNED, COMPRESS_MODE_AFBC), confirmed
  against the Allwinner Decoder Engine Registers Guide.
- Add cedrus_is_afbc_format()/cedrus_dst_is_afbc() helpers and enable the
  AFBC mode bits in cedrus_engine_enable() when the capture format is one
  of the AFBC fourccs.
- Add the 8- and 10-bit AFBC capture formats, scoped to VP9 via
  src_format and placed after the plain formats so P010/NV12 remain the
  default (AFBC is opt-in via S_FMT).
- Size AFBC buffers in cedrus_prepare_format() and skip the 8-bit + 2-bit
  10-bit split for AFBC, which carries full 10-bit samples in its body.

AFBC is a single interleaved buffer, so the existing per-plane address
helper already points both luma and chroma registers at the buffer base
(zero line stride).

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
[aiyengar: rebased onto Armbian's "Implement AFBC YUV420 formats for H265",
 which already adds the VE_MODE compression bits, the AFBC mode setup in
 cedrus_engine_enable(), the cedrus_dst_format_set() case and the AFBC
 sizing in cedrus_prepare_format(); only the VP9 parts are left]
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
